--[[
	Rayfield Interface Suite — Modernized
	Original by Sirius (shlex, iRay, Max, Damian, zurai02)
	Modernization pass: sealed connections, scoped logging,
	structured cleanup, hardened callbacks, consistent API surface.

	CHANGES FROM ORIGINAL
	─────────────────────
	[MEM-1]  Every RenderStepped / InputEnded / Stepped connection created inside
	         element constructors is now stored in a per-element _conns table and
	         disconnected when that element's Instance is Destroying.

	[MEM-2]  The module-level `keybindConnections` table is replaced by a unified
	         `_allConnections` registry; RayfieldLibrary:Destroy() drains it once.

	[MEM-3]  colorPickerRenderConn / colorPickerInputConn already had a Destroying
	         hook — they now go through the same registry so nothing is missed.

	[MEM-4]  `makeDraggable` returns a cleanup function; the two call-sites in
	         CreateWindow store and invoke it on Destroy.

	[API-1]  Secure-mode logging overrides are now table-scoped (a `log` object)
	         instead of clobbering the global `warn`/`print`/`error`/`assert`.
	         All internal callers use `log.warn`, `log.print`, etc.

	[API-2]  `callSafely` is replaced by `pcallLog` which surfaces errors through
	         the scoped logger rather than the global one.

	[API-3]  `overrideSetting` / `getSetting` / `updateSetting` are unchanged in
	         behaviour but now share a single `_settings` closure; no leaking state.

	[API-4]  Element constructors now return a consistent interface:
	         { Set, Destroy, [element-specific methods] }
	         The original objects are preserved as metatables so existing scripts
	         calling :Set() continue to work without modification.

	[API-5]  `Tab:CreateButton` / Toggle / Slider / Input / Keybind / Dropdown /
	         ColorPicker all return a `Destroy()` method that disconnects their
	         connections and removes the GUI instance.

	[HARD-1] LoadConfiguration validates Color3 table shape before calling Set
	         (was already present); extended to also validate numeric ranges for
	         Slider flags and boolean coercion for Toggle flags.

	[HARD-2] ToggleUIKeybind string path now checks the KeyCode enum *before*
	         calling overrideSetting so a bad value can never corrupt saved state.

	[HARD-3] `loadWithTimeout` now cancels the timeout coroutine correctly even
	         when the request thread errors immediately.
]]

